From 4493649ea6f196d47faa4f48169091d9092567e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhixiang Zhao <matthewzhaocc@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:03:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] xfrm: state: don't return an unchecked state from
 xfrm_state_find()

With CONFIG_XFRM_OFFLOAD and a packet offload policy, the bydst and
wildcard walks in xfrm_state_find() stop with a break at the first
software state. x then points at that state, which was never matched
against the template, addresses or selector, and never passed to
xfrm_state_look_at().

Policies without XFRM_POLICY_CPU_ACQUIRE always overwrite x with best.
With XFRM_POLICY_CPU_ACQUIRE, x is set to best only when best belongs to
the current CPU, so x can keep the state from the break. It is then
non-NULL, the new-acquire block is skipped, and the unrelated state is
returned for the flow, with its SPI, keys and, in tunnel mode, its outer
addresses.

Clear x before deciding whether to use best.

Fixes: 1ddf9916ac09 ("xfrm: Add support for per cpu xfrm state handling.")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c b/net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c
index 0555e5d79..836b45777 100644
--- a/net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c
+++ b/net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c
@@ -1517,6 +1517,7 @@ xfrm_state_find(const xfrm_address_t *daddr, const xfrm_address_t *saddr,
 	}
 
 found:
+	x = NULL;
 	if (!(pol->flags & XFRM_POLICY_CPU_ACQUIRE) ||
 	    (best && (best->pcpu_num == pcpu_id)))
 		x = best;

